docs {
  # Group service

  Group keys, relay access tokens and the stream index, served by `backend/cmd/groupd`.

  A group key travels in a request body and never in a path, a key in a URL being a key in every proxy log between the client and here.
  The index is the exception: a GET has no body a cache or a proxy will honour, so it takes its group key in the query.

  Behind the deployment's reverse proxy these routes are paths under the relay's own name, which is why the `Production` environment points `groupService` at that name with no port (`deploy/Caddyfile`).
  A relay reached directly answers them on `groupd`'s own port instead, which is what `Local` names.
}
